  "worked_solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{5}{x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244490/assets/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{5}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244490/assets/7ce9a42f05beeebb422c49e34670513a65a7183a51bd49fb2354e72f0942513e.png)",
